  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (cut from upstream/main 8060358f).\n\n## What changed\n- New MCP tool `edit_machine {patch, setup?}` (`crates/app/src/mcp/machine_tools.rs`): RFC 7396 merge patch over the mounted machine's stored definition (edm section and any other Machine key), applied through the same undoable `LoadMachine` / `SetSetupMachine` the Machine window's Apply uses. One undo step.\n- Refusals by name, nothing changed: new `Edm::refusal()` (post crate, `edm_named.rs`) names the first broken rule (`edm.max_orbit_radius`, `edm.orbits[0].kind`, `edm.conditions[0].id` ...); a wire key on a sinker (or vice versa) is refused; unknown keys are refused as `unknown key 'edm.x'` (not ignored); a no-op patch and a setup without its own machine are refused.\n- `get_job` gains `machine {path, definition}` for read-back.\n- Decision: docs/decisions/1162-mcp-edit-machine.md.\n\n## Tests\n`crates/app/tests/mcp_edit_machine.rs`: an_edm_edit_is_one_undo_step_and_get_job_reads_it_back, a_bad_edit_is_refused_by_name_and_changes_nothing, edit_machine_needs_a_machine_and_a_known_setup. Quick gate green on the final head (post + app suites); clippy -D warnings clean on camcraft-app and camcraft-post.\n\n## Not exercised\n- `edm.codes` from the issue does not exist in this tree (no such field), so nothing was added for it.\n- The per-setup (`setup`) edit path is only covered by its refusals, not a positive case.\n- The camcraft-mcp skill (a process file) is not updated: it should list `edit_machine` and `get_job`'s new `machine` key (maintainer follow-up).\n\nChangelog: MCP edit_machine: merge-patch edit of the mounted machine (incl. the sinker/wire edm section), one undo step, refusals by key; get_job shows the machine (#1162, PR #M)\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1162\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
